# =============================================================
#  Rabbit Grill Khao Yai - what does NOT go in the repo
#
#  Rule of thumb: commit the SOURCE and the PIPELINE, not the
#  raw material it was made from and not what it produces.
#
#  Everything the site actually serves (img/*.jpg, css, js,
#  data, the four pages) IS committed, so a fresh clone runs
#  and rebuilds without any of the files listed below.
# =============================================================

# ---- source material, not source code ----------------------
# The restaurant own menu PDFs and the page scans pulled out of
# them. ~80 MB, and menu-food.pdf alone is 35 MB. The dish
# photos were already cropped out of these into img/, and every
# price already lives in data/menu.json, so nothing downstream
# needs them. Keep the originals in the client folder, off git.
doc/*.pdf
doc/pages/
doc/menu-avocado.jpg
# (doc/RESEARCH.md is tracked - it is the provenance record.)

# ---- QA output ---------------------------------------------
# Screenshots from the headless Edge harness. Regenerated any
# time by _qa\shot.ps1 / _qa\mshot.ps1, and they churn hard.
_qa/shots/
_qa/*.png

# ---- unprocessed photography -------------------------------
# Full-res Facebook originals and the TikTok frame dump. These
# are the input to _qa\extract-venue.ps1; the web-sized JPEGs
# it produced are committed in img/ and are what the site uses.
img/raw/
img/tiktok-*/

# ---- build output ------------------------------------------
# The 8.5 MB single-file artifact. Derived entirely from the
# tracked pages, css, js and img/, so committing it would add
# 8.5 MB of binary churn to history for something that is one
# command away:
#   powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File _qa\build-artifact.ps1
rabbit-grill-artifact.html

# ---- machine noise -----------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.tmp
